{"step_index":1118,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-11T23:33:08Z","thinking":"**Exploring the Candidate Proposition**\n\nInvestigating how to prove the given target, considering the `Candidate` proposition. The `Candidate` involves `GraphCalc.radius G`, which calculates eccentricity. This suggests the proof might involve bounding the radius of a graph.\n\n\n**Analyzing Definitions and Theorems**\n\nExamining the provided definitions, both `radius` and `romanDominationNumber` are defined as the minimum over finite sets, hinting at potential connections through inequalities. The `le_romanDominationNumber` lemma seems crucial for bounding the Roman domination number. `radius_le_eccentricity` provides a direct inequality between radius and eccentricity, which can be useful. The final lemma shows how a condition on the `ballWithin` function bounds the eccentricity.\n\n\n**Simplifying the Target Goal**\n\nThe core problem boils down to proving the existence of a vertex $v$ such that its ball of radius `romanWeight f - 1` covers the entire graph. The condition reduces the target to finding a specific vertex $v$ for a radius around `romanWeight f - 1` that covers the entire graph. The bound on `romanWeight f` gives a specific target.\n\n\n**Connecting Distance to BallWithin**\n\nObserved that the previously tested examples on the atlas show `rad(G) <= romanWeight(f) - 1`. The goal is to find a proof in Lean and using available Mathlib lemmas. Mathlib has `SimpleGraph.dist`, `SimpleGraph.Connected`, and `SimpleGraph.Walk`, and the challenge involves `ballWithin`, which is related to `SimpleGraph.dist`.\n\n**Analyzing Vertex Distances**\n\nVertex 5 on $P_6$ had `ballWithin 3 5 = univ` because it is adjacent to a vertex with label 2, and close to another. Now checking if there ALWAYS exists a vertex with the property `ballWithin (romanWeight f - 1) v = univ`. This aligns with the previous observation.\n\n\n**Connecting ballWithin to Walk Lemmas**\n\nThe key lemma `ballWithin_eq_univ_of_forall_walk` suggests showing `ballWithin G k v = univ` requires demonstrating a walk from $v$ to any $w$ of length $\\le k$. This highlights the direct link between `ballWithin` and graph walks. The target condition relates to showing `ballWithin (romanWeight f - 1) v = univ`. The definition of `ballWithin` is recursive.\n\n\n**Examining Vertex Distances and Radius**\n\nConsidering the implications of the Roman dominating set definition: Every vertex is within distance 1 of a vertex with a non-zero value. This observation suggests the graph's structure is closely tied to the Roman weight and potentially the radius. The case of `radius G <= 1` or `romanWeight f >= |V|` are already handled.\n\n**Analyzing Radius 2 and Roman Weight**\n\nNow considering the case when the graph radius is 2, trying to show `romanWeight f >= 3`. If the `romanWeight f` were less than or equal to 2, it would be exactly 2 because the graph is nontrivial. A `romanWeight` of 2 would imply a vertex with value 2 and all other vertices having value 0.\n\n**Deduction on Roman Domination**\n\nWith only one vertex having a value of 2 and all others 0, for the Roman dominating set property to hold, every vertex must be adjacent to the vertex with the value of 2.  Thus the graph is a star graph. If the radius is 2, a vertex at distance 2 is needed, which is a contradiction.\n\n\n**Formalizing the Roman Domination Lemma**\n\nIf a vertex $u$ has weight 2, and the total Roman weight is 2, then all other vertices $w$ have weight 0. Since the function is Roman dominating, each $w$ must have a neighbor with weight 2, and that can only be $u$, meaning $u$ is adjacent to all other vertices. This implies the radius is at most 1, contradicting the assumption of a radius of 2. If no vertex has weight 2, then the number of vertices is at most 2, which also leads to a radius of 1, a contradiction.\n\n**Reaching a Contradiction**\n\nTherefore, a Roman weight of 2 is impossible if the graph radius is at least 2. This proves that if the radius is 2 or more, the Roman weight must be at least 3. If the radius is exactly 2, then radius + 1 is less than or equal to the Roman weight. This confirms the lower bound of 3 for the Roman weight when the radius equals 2.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"cat << 'EOF' > /mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/handoff/promising13/task_e20263a9/test_weight2.lean\nimport Mathlib\nimport LeanProject.GraphInvariantsComputable\n\nopen SimpleGraph\nopen GraphCalc\n\nlemma ballWithin_one_eq_univ_of_adj_all {V : Type} [Fintype V] [DecidableEq V]\n    (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] (u : V)\n    (h : ∀ w : V, w = u ∨ G.Adj u w) :\n    ballWithin G 1 u = Finset.univ := by\n  ext w\n  simp only [Finset.mem_univ, iff_true]\n  cases h w with\n  | inl heq =>\n    rw [heq]\n    dsimp [ballWithin]\n    exact Finset.mem_union_left _ (Finset.mem_singleton_self u)\n  | inr hadj =>\n    dsimp [ballWithin]\n    apply Finset.mem_union_right\n    rw [Finset.mem_biUnion]\n    use u\n    refine ⟨Finset.mem_singleton_self u, ?_⟩\n    rw [Finset.mem_filter]\n    exact ⟨Finset.mem_univ w, hadj⟩\n\nEOF\n/mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/tools/antigravity/check.sh test_weight2.lean\n","Cwd":"/mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/handoff/promising13/task_e20263a9","WaitMsBeforeAsync":20000,"toolAction":"Testing ballWithin_one_eq_univ_of_adj_all","toolSummary":"Check test_weight2.lean"}}]}
{"step_index":1119,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"RUNNING","created_at":"2026-09-11T23:33:20Z","content":"Created At: 2026-09-12T01:33:20+02:00\nTool is running as a background task with task id: f458c9cf-488d-4cd8-8365-7c4e4b16e3f9/task-1119\nTask Description: cat << 'EOF' > /mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/handoff/promising13/task_e20263a9/test_weight2.lean\nimport Mathlib\nimport LeanProject.GraphInvariantsComputable\n\nopen SimpleGraph\nopen GraphCalc\n\nlemma ballWithin_one_eq_univ_of_adj_all {V : Type} [Fintype V] [DecidableEq V]\n    (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] (u : V)\n    (h : ∀ w : V, w = u ∨ G.Adj u w) :\n    ballWithin G 1 u = Finset.univ := by\n  ext w\n  simp only [Finset.mem_univ, iff_true]\n  cases h w with\n  | inl heq =>\n    rw [heq]\n    dsimp [ballWithin]\n    exact Finset.mem_union_left _ (Finset.mem_singleton_self u)\n  | inr hadj =>\n    dsimp [ballWithin]\n    apply Finset.mem_union_right\n    rw [Finset.mem_biUnion]\n    use u\n    refine ⟨Finset.mem_singleton_self u, ?_⟩\n    rw [Finset.mem_filter]\n    exact ⟨Finset.mem_univ w, hadj⟩\n\nEOF\n/mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/tools/antigravity/check.sh test_weight2.lean\n\nTask logs are available at: file:///tmp/agyhome.NWyWnj/.gemini/antigravity-cli/brain/f458c9cf-488d-4cd8-8365-7c4e4b16e3f9/.system_generated/tasks/task-1119.log\nYOU MUST TAKE ONE OF THE FOLLOWING TWO ACTIONS: A) either proceed to other relevant work (if any) or, B) simply update the user with a short message (that you have launched the command and will wait for it to finish) and end the turn.\n DO NOTHING ELSE."}
