{"step_index":1130,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-11T23:34:07Z","thinking":"**Deducing graph properties**\n\nObserving that if a vertex is adjacent to all other vertices in a graph, the graph's radius is at most 1. Considering the case where the Roman weight of a labeling is 2. Applying the result that if no vertex is labeled 2, the graph's order is at most the Roman weight, it follows that for a non-trivial graph, the order must be exactly 2.\n\n\n**Analyzing radius with Roman weight**\n\nIf a Roman dominating function has weight at most 2, then the graph's radius is at most 1, regardless of whether a vertex has label 2 or not.  Consequently, the contrapositive states that if the radius is at least 2, then the Roman weight must be at least 3. Now, considering a proof by contradiction for the lemma. Assume Roman weight is less than 3, so equal to 2. Considering the case when no vertex has label 2, leading to the graph having at most two vertices.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"cat << 'EOF' >> /mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/handoff/promising13/task_e20263a9/test_weight2.lean\n\nlemma card_le_romanWeight_of_no_two {V : Type} [Fintype V] [DecidableEq V]\n    (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj]\n    (f : V → Fin 3) (hf : GraphCalc.IsRomanDominatingFunction G f)\n    (h_no2 : ∀ v : V, (f v : ℕ) ≠ 2) :\n    Fintype.card V ≤ GraphCalc.romanWeight f := by\n  unfold GraphCalc.romanWeight\n  have h_no0 : ∀ v : V, (f v : ℕ) ≠ 0 := by\n    intro v hv\n    have h_f0 : f v = 0 := by ext; exact hv\n    obtain ⟨u, _, hu2⟩ := hf v h_f0\n    have hu2_nat : (f u : ℕ) = 2 := by rw [hu2]; rfl\n    exact h_no2 u hu2_nat\n  have h_ge1 : ∀ v : V, 1 ≤ (f v : ℕ) := by\n    intro v\n    have h0 := h_no0 v\n    omega\n  have h_sum : ∑ v : V, 1 ≤ ∑ v : V, (f v : ℕ) :=\n    Finset.sum_le_sum (fun v _ => h_ge1 v)\n  rw [Finset.sum_const, nsmul_eq_mul, mul_one] at h_sum\n  rw [Finset.card_univ]